usage: reptor mcp [-h] [--remove-fields REMOVE_FIELDS]
                  [--transport {stdio,sse,streamable-http}] [--host HOST]
                  [--port PORT] [--read-only] [--mcp-debug MCP_DEBUG]

Starts the Model Context Protocol (MCP) server

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --remove-fields REMOVE_FIELDS
                        Comma-separated fields to strip before sending to the LLM. Prefix with finding:, note:, or section:; unprefixed names default to finding (e.g. 'affected_components,note:icon_emoji,section:label')
  --transport {stdio,sse,streamable-http}
                        Transport mode for MCP server (default: stdio). 'sse' is deprecated; prefer 'streamable-http' for remote access.
  --host HOST           Bind address for sse/streamable-http (default: 127.0.0.1). Ignored for stdio.
  --port PORT           Bind port for sse/streamable-http (default: 8000). Ignored for stdio.
  --read-only           Expose only read tools; do not register write/destructive tools (create/patch/delete findings, patch report data, write notes)
  --mcp-debug MCP_DEBUG
                        Path to log file for debugging MCP communication
